        "An underwater-seal chest drain stays below the chest with the tube 2 cm under sterile water; swinging means patency, bubbling on expiration means air leaving and continuous bubbling a leak, bubbling that stops in a breathless patient means a block; drainage is measured and more than 100–200 mL of blood an hour reported; a bubbling drain is never clamped, a disconnected tube goes into sterile water and a drain that falls out is covered with a three-sided dressing.",
