        "Collect, label, store and transport blood, sputum, swab, urine, stool and cerebrospinal fluid specimens correctly, including venepuncture with the order of draw, capillary sampling and blood cultures, and explain why a mislabelled specimen is discarded.",
        "Recognise critical laboratory results — potassium, sodium, glucose, haemoglobin, platelets, positive cultures and malaria films — and act on them with the right urgency, including the read-back and documentation of a telephoned result.",
        "Prepare, position, support and monitor a patient for a lumbar puncture, pleural aspiration, paracentesis, bone marrow aspiration and liver biopsy, and provide the care that follows each.",
